        "uuid": "886bba3e_867e35b1",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 971,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-08T07:51:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The code below only works for prefix \u003d\u003d 24, even though it seems to take a generic prefixLen as input.\n\nBefore PrivateAddressCoordinator is available, I\u0027m wondering if it would be cleaner to just rotate on 3-4 hardcoded prefixes, instead of trying to replicate what PrivateAddressCoordinator should do (which is difficult esp. if you consider variable prefix length).\n\nSo:\n - setChangePrefixOnDecline(isTetheringNcm \u0026\u0026 NCM_PREFIXES.contains(serverLinkAddr)) to make sure this behavior is not used from other prefixes\n - in handleNewPrefixRequest, use something like:\n\n// TODO: use PrivateAddressCoordinator instead of this temporary logic\noldIndex \u003d Arrays.asList(NCM_PREFIXES).indexOf(oldPrefix);\nif (oldIndex \u003d\u003d -1) // error\nnewPrefix \u003d NCM_PREFIXES[(oldIndex + 1) % NCM_PREFIXES.length];",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 971,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 971,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "e8033f0477cb009fab682c725fd251e577a5714d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59c959d2_dcbd8151",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 971,
      "author": {
        "id": 1406251
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-12T03:43:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that would be simpler to just rotate on 4 hardcoded prefixes. Replaced this logic with hardcoded list.\n\nDo we need to check NCM_PREFIXES.contains(serverLinkAddr)?\n    - since every time we just pick the next prefix from the prefixes list, this should be always true.\n    - after we introduce PrivateAddressCoordinator.requestDownstreamPrefix, here NCM_PREFIXES will be removed finally as well.\n\nThought?",
      "parentUuid": "886bba3e_867e35b1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 971,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 971,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "e8033f0477cb009fab682c725fd251e577a5714d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "87c039d1_69405e82",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 971,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-12T13:04:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s less guarantee that it\u0027s true the first time IpServer receives CMD_NEW_PREFIX_REQUEST, as the \"CMD_NEW_PREFIX_REQUEST is only received when type is NCM\" guarantee is ensured in startDhcp, so a separate part of the code that could be changed without noticing the mismatch. \nIt\u0027s true that after introducing PrivateAddressCoordinator, that may not be necessary anymore though.\n\nPrivateAddressCoordinator will need to use the tethering type in requestDownstreamPrefix, so I think you can add a tetheringType parameter to handleNewPrefixRequest and requestDownstreamAddress, and fail if that parameter is not TYPE_NCM. Then the parameter will already be here when switching to PrivateAddressCoordinator.\n\nI see you have a check that the current prefix is in the NCM_PREFIXES list though, which is roughly equivalent to that. So current code LGTM without adding the parameter.",
      "parentUuid": "59c959d2_dcbd8151",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 971,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 971,
        "endChar": 18
      },
