    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cfcf0188_6fbc1294",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 989,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-12T13:04:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "L.814 calls networkAddInterface, but setupTetherInterface seems to do more stuff (tetherInterfaceAdd, networkAddInterface, addRoutesToLocalNetwork)\n\ntetherInterfaceAdd in particular seems to add the interface to a list:\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:system/netd/server/TetherController.cpp;drc\u003ddde0c026a156858d0ac6df5ae08118f46a9a681b;l\u003d493\n\nIf I read this right this would cause the list to get additional duplicate entries ?\n\nDo you really need to go through the \"add interface\" part considering that the interface is already configured as a tethered interface ? If you don\u0027t call untetherInterface, It seems that just calling addRoutesToLocalNetwork instead of setupTetherInterface would be enough, since the interface is already setup.",
      "parentUuid": "d6f1862d_d4dd2848",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 989,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 989,
        "endChar": 33
      },
      "revId": "e8033f0477cb009fab682c725fd251e577a5714d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28f33d6b_b15a0c5e",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/android/net/ip/IpServer.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 989,
      "author": {
        "id": 1406251
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-05-13T14:54:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, you are right. Actually I had a debug and confirmed with Mark, tetherInterfaceAdd also does applyDnsInterface to notify dnsmasq listen on the interface bound with IPv4 address. This is required when we applying a new generated IPv4 address on the interface, otherwise, that results DNS validation failure problem although appropriate routes have been configured.\n\nInstead of calling tetherInterfaceAdd which might put the same interface in the end of interface list, we can just call Netd.tetherApplyDnsInterface, that has the same behavior and avoid messing up the interface list. Then we don\u0027t bother to call untetherInterface first and follow tetherInterfaece neither.",
      "parentUuid": "cfcf0188_6fbc1294",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 989,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 989,
        "endChar": 33
      },
